===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|alighten|t=to descend from a place: to dismount, get off; to descend to a place: to arrive or stop (at a place); to land; to drop; to attack; of lightning: to strike; to leap on to, mount; to descend in rank; to cause (someone) to lose rank; to come forth, spring from; to alleviate, relieve; (''Christianity'') of Jesus: to come down to earth from heaven, become incarnate; to descend (to hell); of the Holy Spirit, angels, miracles, etc.: to descend (from heaven); to descend (upon someone); to appear in a place}}{{nb...|aliȝt, aliȝte, aliȝth, alight, alighte, aliht, alihte, allight, allighten, alliȝt, allyght, allyhte, alyȝt, alyȝte, alyght, alyghte, alyht, alyhte|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=alighten|pos=''v.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED1123}}</ref> from a merger of:<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=5024|date=December 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=alight{{sup|1}}|pos=v}}</ref>

* {{inh|en|ang|ālīhtan|t=to alight, dismount}}, from {{m|ang|ā-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘away, from, off, out’}} + {{m|ang|līhtan}}, {{m|ang|līehtan|t=to descend, alight, light; to make easy or light, alleviate, lighten, relieve}}, ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₁lengʷʰ-|t=not heavy, light}}; and
* {{inh|en|ang|ġelīhtan|t=to descend; to come down, dismount; to make easy or light, alleviate, lighten, relieve}}, from {{m|ang|ġe-|pos={{glossary|intensifier|intensifying}} prefix, attached to {{glossary|verb}}s to indicate completeness or perfection}} + {{m|ang|līhtan}}, {{m|ang|līehtan}} (see above).

The English word is analyzable as {{prefix|en|a|pos1=prefix meaning ‘away, from, off, out’|light|t2=to ease, lighten; to take off; to unload; to dismount; (''archaic'') to come down, land; to dismount}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
* {{cog|gml|erlichten|t=to lighten}}
* {{cog|goh|gilīhten|t=to make less heavy, lighten}} ({{cog|gmh|gelīhten}}); {{cog|goh|irlīhten|t=to alleviate}} ({{cog|gmh|erlīhten}}, modern {{cog|de|erleichten}})
