##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=IV|page=105|lines=395–397|passage=Then from his loftie ſtand on that high Tree / Down he '''alights''' among the ſportful Herd / Of thoſe fourfooted kindes, himſelf now one, {{...}}|year=1873}}
##* {{RQ:Homer Pope Iliad|volume=VI|book=XXIII|pages=108–109|pageref=108|lines=1038–1041|passage=The wounded Bird, e'er yet ſhe breath'd her laſt, / With flagging Wings '''alighted''' on the Maſt, / A Moment hung, and ſpread her Pinions there, / Then ſudden dropt, and left her Life in Air.}}
