===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*lewk-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is probably derived partly:<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|2}}|noformat=1|id=5026|date=December 2021}}</ref>

* from {{inh|en|enm|alighten|t=to kindle, light, set on fire; to begin burning; to become bright, shine; to arouse, rouse, stir; (''figuratively'') to enlighten spiritually, illuminate}}{{nb...|aliȝt, aliȝte, aliȝtte, alihte, aliʒth, allyght, alyghte, alyȝt, alyȝte|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=alighten|pos=''v.''(2)|noformat=1|id=MED1124}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|ālīhtan}}, {{m|ang|ālȳhtan|t=to light up; enlighten}} (perhaps modelled after {{noncog|la|illūmināre}}, the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|active}} {{glossary|infinitive}} of {{m|la|illūminō|t=to brighten, illuminate, light up}}), from {{m|ang|ā-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘away, from, off, out’}} + {{m|ang|līhtan}}, {{m|ang|līehtan|t=to glow, to shine; to illuminate, to light}} (ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*lewk-|t=to see; to shine; bright}}); and
* from {{inh|en|enm|onlighten|t=to cause (something) to shine; to clarify; (''figuratively'') to enlighten spiritually}}{{nb...|onlight, onlihte, onlihten|otherforms=1}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=onlighten|pos=''v.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED30647}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|onlīhtan}}, a variant of {{m|ang|inlīhtan|t=to give light to, brighten, illuminate; to cause to shine; to shine; (''figuratively'') to give clear sight; to clear a mental fog, enlighten}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*inliuhtijaną|t=to enlighten, illumine}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*in|t=in; into}} + {{m|gem-pro|*liuhtijaną|t=to give light, shine}} (ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*lewk-}}; see above); and
* from later uses of {{m|en|alight|pos=adjective}}.

The English word is analysable as {{prefix|en|a|pos1=prefix meaning ‘away, from, off, out’|light|t2=to start (a fire); to burn, set fire to; to become ignited, take fire; to provide light, illuminate; to show the way by means of a light}}.

The {{glossary|adjective}} and {{glossary|adverb}} are derived from Late {{inh|en|enm|alight|pos=adjective}}{{nb...|aliȝht, aliȝt, aliȝthe, alyȝt|otherforms=1}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ālīht}}, {{m|ang|ālȳht}},<ref name="OED"/> a {{glossary|past}} {{glossary|participle}} form of {{inh|en|ang|ālīhtan}}, {{m|ang|ālȳhtan|pos=verb}} (see above); but have also been subsequently interpreted as {{prefix|en|a|pos1=prefix meaning ‘at; in; on’, used to show a condition, manner, or state|light|t2=not dark or obscure, bright, clear; highly luminous}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''adv|id=5022|date=December 2021|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|alt=alight{{sup|2}}|pos=adj}}</ref>

