#: {{ux|en|In this street, the shops '''always''' close during lunchtime.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1840|author={{w|Edward Bulwer-Lytton, 1st Baron Lytton|Edward Bulwer-Lytton}}|title={{w|Money (play)|Money}}
|passage=His liveries are black,&mdash;his carriage is black,&mdash;he '''always''' rides a black galloway,&mdash;and, faith, if he ever marry again, I think he will show his respect to the sainted Maria by marrying a black woman.}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that '''always''' grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=w:Michael Arlen|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1519647W “Piracy”: A Romantic Chronicle of These Days]|chapter=Ep./1/1
|passage=And so it had '''always''' pleased M. Stutz to expect great things from the dark young man whom he had first seen in his early twenties ; and his expectations has waxed rather than waned on hearing the faint bruit of the love of Ivor and Virginia—for Virginia, M. Stutz thought, would bring fineness to a point in a man like Ivor Marlay,{{nb...}}.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=7|passage=The highway to the East Coast which ran through the borough of Ebbfield had '''always''' been a main road and even now, despite the vast garages, the pylons and the gaily painted factory glasshouses which had sprung up beside it, there still remained an occasional trace of past cultures.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Feb 81|volume=8|number=29|journal=Gay Community News|page=8|title=Voices in the Night|author=Andrea Loewenstein|text=She used to '''always''' talk about how she wished she had time to write all day, but now she ''had'' the time, she never even went near the typewriter.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} if necessary, or if there is no better option; [[in any event]].
#: {{syn|en|anyhow|anyway|at any rate|regardless|Thesaurus:regardless}}
#: {{ux|en|I thought I could '''always''' go back to work.}}

====Usage notes====
* Used for both duration and frequency.
* "Always" used with a continuous tense can imply anger or annoyance about another person's persistent habits, for example "My mum is always telling me to tidy me room!".

