#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1977|author=w:Barry Hannah|title=Coming Close to Donna|journal=[[w:Esquire (magazine)|Esquire]]|location=New York, N.Y.|page=76|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Em5XAAAAYAAJ&q=%22her+always%22|column=2|issn=0194-9535|oclc=824603960|passage=I am her '''always''' and she is my '''always''' and that’s the whole trouble. For two years I tried to make her pregnant.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=6 May 2001|author=Lord Usher|title=I hate Willow. ("Tough Love" spoilers)|newsgroup=alt.tv.buffy-v-slayer|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251207150454/https://groups.google.com/g/alt.tv.buffy-v-slayer/c/bpY6qxxJuB4/m/wKnzk6RFS3kJ|passage=What we saw was cute-'n'-cuddly Willow, takin' care of her girl and spouting nauseating platitudes like "You're my '''always'''."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Scarlett Dawn|chapter=8|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-FK8DAAAQBAJ&pg=PT101|title=The King Trilogy: Forever Evermore Books 1-3|location=Sydney, N.S.W.|publisher=Escape Publishing/{{w|Harlequin Enterprises}}|isbn=9781489221148|passage=“Same with me. I love Gideon. He’s my '''always''', but as far as true friendships go,” she cleared her throat, “I’ve never met three people I click with better.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Tara Sosa|title=The Beauty Series|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=pCbHDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT1328|year_published=2019|id=ASIN B0835R25F1|passage=He is my everything too. He’s my '''always''' too.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=29 August 2017|author=w:Mariah Stewart|chapter=Epilogue|title=The Chesapeake Bride|series=Chesapeake Diaries|seriesvolume=11|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Pocket Books|page=364|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=60MyDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA364|isbn=978-1-5011-5435-5|passage=Every once in a while Cass took off the wide gold band he’d slipped on her finger and read the inscription: ''My everything and my '''always'''. My Chesapeake bride.''}}
#* {{quote-web|en|year=2020|author=John Mangum|title=Les nuits d’été (Hector Berlioz)|work=LA Phil|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200806012607/https://www.laphil.com/musicdb/pieces/2226/les-nuits-dete|location=Los Angeles, Calif.|publisher=w:Los Angeles Philharmonic|passage=When performed as a cycle, the songs convey this loss all the more strongly, not just as individual compositions touched by melancholy, but as a coherent conception, one where the longed-for "'''always'''" of the first song, "Villanelle," becomes unattainable in the last one, "L'île inconnue." Berlioz' rapturous, idealistic love for Harriet had faded - the breeze had blown his ship on a course far from one leading to the "'''always'''" of his youthful dreams.}}

