==English==

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:ambicioun|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂en-}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁ey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ambicioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|ambition}}, from {{der|en|la|ambitiō||ambition, a striving for favor, literally 'a going around', especially of candidates for office in Rome soliciting votes}}, from {{m|la|ambiō||to go around, solicit votes}}. See [[ambient]], [[issue]]. {{surf|en|ambit|-ion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/æmˈbɪʃ.ən/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/æmˈbɪʃ.ən/|[ɛəmˈbɪʃ.n̩]|a=GA,CA|q2=/æ/ raising}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-ambition.ogg|a=California}}
* {{IPA|en|/æmˈbɪʃ.ən/|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɛmˈbəʃ.ən/|a=NZ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} [[eager|Eager]] or [[inordinate]] [[desire]] for some object that confers [[distinction]], as preferment, honor, superiority, political power, or fame; desire to distinguish one's self from other people.
#: {{ux|en|My daughter, Johanna, wants to be a firefighter very much. She has a lot of '''ambition'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Works|chapter=VII|page=270|volume=IV|passage=The third part of practice hath divers branches, but one principal root in these our times, which is the vast and overspreading '''ambition''' and usurpation of the see of Rome; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Burke Natural Society|page=20|passage=One is aſtoniſhed hovv ſuch a ſmall ſpot could furniſh Men ſufficient to ſacrifice to the pitiful '''Ambition''' of poſſeſſing five or ſix thouſand more Acres, or tvvo or three more Villages: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1997|title=w:Paranoid Android|album=w:OK Computer|artist=w:Radiohead|passage='''Ambition''' makes you look pretty ugly / Kicking, squealing, Gucci little piggy}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An object of an ardent desire.
#: {{ux|en|My '''ambition''' is to own a helicopter.}}
# A desire, as in (sense 1), for another person to achieve these things.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A personal quality similar to [[motivation]], not necessarily tied to a single goal.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of going about to solicit or obtain an office, or any other object of desire; [[canvass]]ing.
#* {{RQ:Milton Samson|page=22|passage=I on th' other ſide / Us'd no '''ambition''' to commend my deeds, {{...}}}}

