#* {{quote-web|en|author=Gaspar Forteza|title=Regarding Simón y otros: Accountability in Argentina and International Human Rights as Domestic Positive Law|url=https://ecollections.law.fiu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1036&context=lawreview|year=Fall 2007|page=187, 229|work=w:FIU Law Review|volume=3|number=1|issn=2643-7759|passage=Shortly after the end of military rule in 1983, the Argentinean National Congress passed legislation that effectively '''amnestied''' many persons who allegedly committed human rights violations such as torture, extra-judicial killing, and forced disappearance. {{...}} In other words, a government may be justified in '''amnestying''' military actions because the alternative would result in the destruction of the democratic state.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200703025608/https://ecollections.law.fiu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1036&context=lawreview}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Stephen Collinson and Maegan Vazquez|title=Trump’s offer of temporary protection for immigrants to end shutdown is a ‘non-starter,’ say Democrats|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/01/19/politics/house-democrats-border-security-funding-trump|date=2019-01-19|passage=“100 miles of border wall in exchange for '''amnestying''' millions of illegals. So if we grant citizenship to a BILLION foreigners, maybe we can finally get a full border wall,” Coulter wrote in another tweet.|quotee=w:Ann Coulter|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108000918/https://edition.cnn.com/2019/01/19/politics/house-democrats-border-security-funding-trump/}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Radina Gigova|title=Amnesty regrets ‘distress’ caused by report on Ukrainian military, but stands by findings|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/08/europe/amnesty-ukraine-military-report-intl|date=2022-08-08|passage=“This is such immoral selectivity,” he added. “Anyone who '''amnesties''' Russia and who artificially creates a such informational context where some attacks by terrorists are supposedly justified or supposedly understandable cannot fail to understand that, in doing so, they are helping the terrorists.”|quotee=w:Volodymyr Zelenskyy|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220820052858/https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/08/europe/amnesty-ukraine-military-report-intl/}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Zachary B. Wolf|title=The 2024 primary campaigns have already changed the Republican Party|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/11/politics/republicans-primaries-policies-what-matters|date=2024-01-11|passage=“The number of people that will be '''amnestied''' when I’m president is zero,” DeSantis said, when asked if he would allow any of the 10 million to stay in the US.|quotee=w:Ron DeSantis|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240312114206/https://www.cnn.com/2024/01/11/politics/republicans-primaries-policies-what-matters}}

