===Etymology===
{{word|en|ine|h₂éd}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{der|en|la-med|affidavit||he has sworn}}, the third person singular perfect tense of {{m|la|affido||swear}}, from {{m|la|fīdō}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-||to command, to persuade, to trust}}. Cognate to {{m|en|fidelity}} and {{m|en|faith}} (same Latin root), but not to {{m|en|affirm}} (shared Latin {{m|la|ad-}} prefix, but different Latin and Proto-Indo-European roots).

